403", "member": "1988", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 10, 1]], "date-time": "2024-10-01T20:37:13Z", "timestamp": 1727815033000}, "score": 30.506725, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://linkresolver.bsigroup.com/junction/resolve/000000000000000000?restype=series&lookup=BS+8468"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3403/bs8468"}, {"institution": [{"name": "Nanyang Technological University"}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 4, 3]], "date-time": "2022-04-03T23:02:30Z", "timestamp": 1649026950951}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Nanyang Technological University", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.32657/10356/5421", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 2]], "date-time": "2019-10-02T16:24:40Z", "timestamp": 1570033480000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2005]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Behaviour-based physical agents as information display devices"], "prefix": "10.32657", "author": [{"given": "Shusong", "family": "Xing", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "13751", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 2]], "date-time": "2019-10-02T16:24:40Z", "timestamp": 1570033480000}, "score": 30.149387, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://hdl.handle.net/10356/5421"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.32657/10356/5421"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 10]], "date-time": "2026-06-10T15:44:04Z", "timestamp": 1781106244669, "version": "3.54.1"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "IGI Global", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781605660547", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9781605660554", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2009]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Among traditional users of Web resources, industry has a growing set of smart industrial devices with embedded intelligence. Just like humans, they need online services (i.e., for condition monitoring, remote diagnostics, maintenance, etc.). In this paper, we present one possible implementation framework for such Web services. Such services should be Semantic Web enabled and form a Service Network based on internal and external agents\u2019 platforms, which can host heterogeneous mobile agents and coordinate them to perform needed tasks. The concept of a \u201cmobile service component\u201d assumes not only exchanging queries and service responses, but also delivering and composition of a service provider. Mobile service component carrier (agent) can move to a field device\u2019s local environment (embedded agent platform) and perform its activities locally. Service components improve their performance through online learning and communication with other components. Heterogeneous service components\u2019 discovery is based on semantic P2P search.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.4018/978-1-60566-054-7.ch054", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2011, 5, 24]], "date-time": "2011-05-24T13:44:10Z", "timestamp": 1306244650000}, "page": "630-641", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Semantic Web Services for Smart Devices Based on Mobile Agents"], "prefix": "10.4018", "author": [{"given": "Vagan", "family": "Terziyan", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Jyvaskyla, Finland"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "2432", "container-title": ["Mobile Computing"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.igi-global.com/viewtitle.aspx?TitleId=26536", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2019, 1, 14]], "date-time": "2019-01-14T13:52:26Z", "timestamp": 1547473946000}, "score": 29.919676, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://services.igi-global.com/reso